    <node id="&quot;AGATHA CHRISTIE (CID:153)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agatha Christie is a renowned author known for her detective novels, including 'Murder on the Orient Express,' which features this narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie is identified with a citation ID as the author of 'Murder on the Orient Express', indicating her role in creating this literary work."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie is the author of 'Murder on the Orient Express,' a detective novel featuring Hercule Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie is the author of 'Murder on the Orient Express,' a novel containing this text as part of its narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie is the author of 'Murder on the Orient Express,' creating the narrative involving characters like M. Bouc, Poirot, and others."&lt;SEP&gt;"Author of 'Murder on the Orient Express', which is the source text for this mystery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Author of 'Murder on the Orient Express,' setting the narrative context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to Agatha Christie as the author of 'Murder on the Orient Express,' where this narrative originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the author Agatha Christie, whose work 'Murder on the Orient Express' is the source text for this narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author and publisher entity associated with the book 'Murder on the Orient Express,' which is the source text of this narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author of 'Murder on the Orient Express,' referenced within the context, providing narrative structure to the mystery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fd65fe3716ce22231f6ea5162982b25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b935beff32f900e8b2f9a059a1a90d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70add9ec68a4e0f891845ba07b41bdc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05861ce1d97b51ee7ba7e14ad6a716ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7a4bf22d1e71c2aa1f0dd57e612483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c80e358e965dae0d3f3898628b68de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af707c4982d5d13c07eb2929dad417be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a74ad1f7a65a442e84243a05d21bd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE TAURUS EXPRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Taurus Express is a train route mentioned as having passengers including a young French lieutenant and Hercule Poirot."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALEPPO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A geographical location mentioned in connection with an overheard conversation relevant to the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aleppo is a location in Syria where the Taurus Express stops, setting the scene for the departure of its important passenger, M. Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aleppo is identified as the current location of the train platform observed by Mary Debenham."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b5b38b2dd23c77b4817324b15fd3d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE GENERAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The General is a high-ranking French military officer who expresses gratitude towards Hercule Poirot for saving the honor of the French Army and averting bloodshed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIEUTENANT DUBOSC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lieutenant Dubosc is a young French officer assigned to see off M. Poirot from Aleppo on the Taurus Express, performing his duties with zeal despite limited knowledge of the situation's background."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lieutenant Dubosc is responsible for seeing off M. Poirot by the Taurus Express, demonstrating enthusiasm and dedication as a young officer with a promising career."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE WAGON LIT CONDUCTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Wagon Lit uniform found in one of the toilets is linked to the murder's appearance as an outside job, pointing towards misdirection in the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Wagon Lit Conductor is one of several individuals providing evidence, likely involved with the train journey narrative."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd65fe3716ce22231f6ea5162982b25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE SECRETARY&quot;">
