    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COUNT AND COUNTESS ANDRENYI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Count and Countess Andrenyi are mentioned as sources of evidence, indicating their involvement in significant events within the narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Count and Countess Andrenyi are characters implicated in a murder case. They are subjects of suspicion by detective Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Count and Countess Andrenyi are passengers on the Orient Express; part of the group being interviewed by Poirot regarding a murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Count and Countess are passengers whose passports contained a grease spot deemed significant by Poirot."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a3febbe10401ac2c84958f17348e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MR. HARDMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A character providing an eyewitness account of events aboard the Orient Express, involved in security and observation duties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Initially introduced as Cyrus Bethman Hardman, a traveling salesman turned private detective from the McNeil Detective Agency tasked with protecting S. E. Ratchett."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Hardman is a character who displays affability and shares his perspectives on American culture with Poirot and M. Bouc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Hardman is a first-class passenger on the Orient Express, subject to questioning by Poirot as part of the murder investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Hardman is an American detective on the train, impressed by Poirot's deductive abilities but initially unable to solve the mystery himself."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Hardman provides evidence regarding the protection of Mr. Ratchett, which Poirot finds questionable due to its implausibility concerning security measures taken during travel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Hardman provides evidence, potentially linked to an event or interaction central to the plot."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70add9ec68a4e0f891845ba07b41bdc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee68b60e91d3765c877c8570ac90496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f56d007fba699897f7e8d88951c40f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc7f212f7cc245171a145500065be35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739553f4722a651ef8fe4bd2726b6a2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE ITALIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A passenger with urgent business in Milan, expressing concern over the train delay."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Italian's evidence contributes to the unfolding story or investigation being depicted in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97f221cfcb44e82fc16604e8188110e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISS DEBENHAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A character who is confirmed as 'all right' by Colonel Arbuthnot in terms of being involved or suspicious in a crime context."&lt;SEP&gt;"A young English lady from Baghdad, characterized by her poise, efficiency, and independence. She interacts with Colonel Arbuthnot during the journey."&lt;SEP&gt;"A young English lady suspected by Poirot of involvement in a crime due to her composure and intelligence; she has alibis provided by strangers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham appears to be acquainted with Colonel Arbuthnot, suggesting a familiarity that contradicts their supposed meeting timeline, indicating potential deception in her testimony."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham is an English lady traveling with Greta Ohlsson, mentioned in relation to her compartment on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham is an English passenger on the train who shares her route from Baghdad with Colonel Arbuthnot and is discussed as part of the investigation by Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham is another passenger tied to the letter H, possessing a dainty linen handkerchief instead of an expensive one."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham is another passenger whose interactions are investigated by Poirot for clues related to the murder case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham is involved as a provider of evidence, playing a role in the narrative’s development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham is one of the passengers who witnessed the mythical woman in the red kimono, adding to the confusion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham is one of the second-class passengers on the Orient Express, involved in Poirot's line of inquiry about the murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham witnessed the woman in a red kimono and her testimony adds to the mystery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham, whose second name is Hermione, is implicated due to her connection with the initial 'H' and other suspicions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ef2a5be101e1bcbe764f5cc6a651113&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c80e358e965dae0d3f3898628b68de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0262591c0f7139618aa8ff97ba9028ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2f47e7e728fa86cdbd201b3054b4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73450c21b26b1c97cae9c9cc4f33121&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b5b38b2dd23c77b4817324b15fd3d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6002972d88a92a390f28d441cd83a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a3febbe10401ac2c84958f17348e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab40254b7af0225a39e56ce1256063e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE GERMAN LADY’S-MAID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hildegarde Schmidt, a German lady's-maid serving on the Orient Express; interviewed by Poirot for information related to Ratchett's murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"The German Lady’s-Maid offers testimony that aids in the progression of the investigation or story arc."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b5b38b2dd23c77b4817324b15fd3d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M. HERCULE POIROT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M. Hercule Poirot is a detective travelling to Stamboul (Istanbul) for leisure after completing a mission, engaging in polite conversation with Lieutenant Dubosc and preparing for his journey."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAURUS EXPRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A train journey that passengers are part of, which is delayed by heavy snowfall in Jugo-Slavia."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Taurus Express is the train that M. Poirot is traveling on from Syria towards Constantinople (now Istanbul), serving as a setting for interactions among characters such as M. Poirot, Lieutenant Dubosc, and Mary Debenham."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97f221cfcb44e82fc16604e8188110e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAMBOUL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stamboul is the location of a missionary school where Greta Ohlsson works as a matron."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stamboul, known today as Istanbul, is the city where M. Poirot plans to stay as a tourist after disembarking from the Taurus Express, marking an important part of his journey."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73450c21b26b1c97cae9c9cc4f33121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARY DEBENHAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A governess who sits with two women at a table, characterized by her cautious demeanor and discreet appearance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A passenger noted for her patience and strong character; interacts with Poirot about other passengers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mary Debenham has no known motive but had her alibi vouched by Greta Ohlsson; she also had suspicious circumstances involving an overheard conversation and refusal to explain it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mary Debenham is a character who interacts with Colonel Arbuthnot and leaves the restaurant car, indicating her role in the scene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mary Debenham is a passenger and former governess involved with Colonel Arbuthnot, questioned by Poirot about her possible involvement in Ratchett's murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mary Debenham is a passenger who appears calm and indifferent during the search of her belongings, showing observation towards Poirot’s actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mary Debenham is initially suspected of involvement in the events on the train but is later defended by Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mary Debenham is traveling on the Taurus Express from Baghdad and is characterized by her fatigue, curiosity about her surroundings, and observations of other passengers such as Lieutenant Dubosc and M. Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mary Debenheim works with Hector MacQueen on planning and executing an intricate scheme involving multiple conspirators against Cassetti."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miss Debenham, also known as Mary, is a passenger on the Orient Express whose interactions and statements are scrutinized by Poirot for clues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c02cf2a88ee1b375e65a1e1e19c6b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e00f6f5a5a46007fccdffb363d3da9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e4b0cbed28fb17eaddac7f89bea44ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2377471b4daac2b86e49ff3b3cd311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ee36d6bef7ec1eb1413cc372b39bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6002972d88a92a390f28d441cd83a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f5533179a24abef3edb831a2667e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97f221cfcb44e82fc16604e8188110e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAGON LIT CONDUCTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A conductor in brown uniform responsible for guiding M. Bouc and Hercule Poirot to their compartment on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"A conductor responsible for a sleeping-car service, mentioned as someone Poirot might be considering in his assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Wagon Lit Conductor, described as a tall sallow man of middle age in brown uniform, manages passenger arrangements on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Wagon Lit conductor assists with boarding procedures and ensures passengers like M. Poirot are comfortable, displaying professionalism during their interactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The train conductor who helps access M. Ratchett's locked compartment and reports the crime to Poirot."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8c80f04908bd81829962c824002084f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828593a23e34b4ef40681f2f1551531c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f52cbd857b4ec571997368d76d3ad4f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAGHDAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A city from which Miss Debenham, a companion of Greta Ohlsson, traveled on the Orient Express."&lt;SEP&gt;"Baghdad is the city from which Mary Debenham begins her journey on the Taurus Express, indicating a starting point in her travel itinerary."&lt;SEP&gt;"The city where Miss Debenham served as a governess, mentioned during conversations between her and Colonel Arbuthnot."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0262591c0f7139618aa8ff97ba9028ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73450c21b26b1c97cae9c9cc4f33121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIRKUK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kirkuk is mentioned as part of Mary Debenham's recent travels before boarding the train to Stamboul (Istanbul)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOSUL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mosul is referenced where Mary stayed at a Rest House, marking another location in her travel history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONEL FROM INDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Colonel from India is one of the few passengers traveling with M. Poirot on the Taurus Express, representing an international passenger demographic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNG ENGLISH LADY FROM BAGHDAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A young English woman from Baghdad shares travel space with M. Poirot and others on the Taurus Express, adding to the diverse group of passengers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871</data>
    </node>
