    <node id="&quot;MR. RATCHETT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An elderly man with a seemingly respectable appearance but who arouses suspicion in Hercule Poirot due to his eyes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Ratchett is a passenger on the train who was involved in the Armstrong kidnapping case as a principal instigator, unbeknownst to his valet Masterman."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Ratchett is an individual whose compartment is being searched by Poirot; his belongings are central to the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Ratchett was a passenger on the Orient Express who was last seen alive by Greta Ohlsson reading a book before being murdered."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Ratchett, whose real identity is later revealed as Cassetti, the man responsible for the Armstrong kidnap case, was murdered on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ratchett is a passenger on the train who appears nervous and causes Mrs. Hubbard's fear."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ratchett is the murdered employer whose death is central to the investigation. He did not reveal his past attempt to engage Poirot's services to MacQueen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sits facing Poirot, noted for his unprepossessing appearance with false benevolence and cruel eyes. A character of interest to M. Bouc and Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"The victim whose murder is central to the investigation, possibly known by Colonel Arbuthnot."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e00f6f5a5a46007fccdffb363d3da9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c80f04908bd81829962c824002084f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05861ce1d97b51ee7ba7e14ad6a716ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7a4bf22d1e71c2aa1f0dd57e612483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73450c21b26b1c97cae9c9cc4f33121&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af707c4982d5d13c07eb2929dad417be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c2fe5c17ad711c386f6cdce1c5b966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a74ad1f7a65a442e84243a05d21bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab40254b7af0225a39e56ce1256063e</data>
    </node>
