      <data key="d1">"An American passenger found dead, stabbed multiple times in his berth."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Ratchett appears to be a victim of a stabbing incident discussed in the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Ratchett is a passenger aboard the Orient Express, whose murder is central to the investigation; he was known to speak no French."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Ratchett is a passenger on the train who has been murdered during the journey."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Ratchett is a passenger whose murder forms the central event of the investigation on the Orient Express."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Ratchett is a victim in 'Murder on the Orient Express,' whose death triggers the investigation led by Hercule Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Ratchett is the victim whose murder sets off the mystery that Poirot needs to solve."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Ratchett was a victim who mentioned being in danger, providing context for Poirot's investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Ratchett, possibly threatened by a suspicious individual disguised as a woman or another man in disguise, is central to the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ratchett is a passenger on the Orient Express who was murdered; details about his habits and behavior are provided by his valet."</data>
