    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEF DE TRAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A large man in blue uniform, present during the discovery of M. Ratchett's body."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chef de Train is an individual on the train who suggested that a woman might be responsible for the murder based on the nature of the crime."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chef de Train provides insights into the murder, suggesting it was committed by a woman based on his observations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The chef de train, who is referenced by other characters, suggesting a role or insight related to the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The individual responsible for overseeing the dining car and assisting with Poirot’s investigation by bringing Mr. MacQueen into the carriage."</data>
