    <node id="&quot;HECTOR MACQUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hector MacQueen corroborates Colonel Arbuthnot’s account of the conductor passing their carriage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hector MacQueen is M. Ratchett's secretary, providing information about his employer and the events surrounding the murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hector MacQueen is Mr. Ratchett's secretary who reveals his knowledge about Mr. Ratchett’s true identity as Cassetti."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hector MacQueen is a key planner in the execution plot and had feelings for Sonia, Susanne's daughter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hector MacQueen is a passenger on the Orient Express, jokingly considered suspicious by himself and others in the context of inheritance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hector MacQueen is eliminated as a suspect based on his physical height and related evidence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hector MacQueen is eliminated as a suspect based on his physical height, which does not match the requirements of certain disguises involved in the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hector MacQueen is the young man who worked for Samuel Edward Ratchett as a secretary or courier and has mixed feelings about his employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hector MacQueen, who adored Sonia (Countess Andrenyi's daughter), works with Mary on the details of an elaborate plan involving multiple individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-90462864ccc3552f8203a4d315744169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e2be2103dbf9128ae4cbba4b8804c3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b935beff32f900e8b2f9a059a1a90d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857357aeeee56eaf90ec14021d2a1053</data>
    </node>
