    <node id="&quot;COUNTESS ANDRENYI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A passenger on the Orient Express whose belongings might contain clues relevant to the murder case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Countess Andrenyi is a passenger who has been successfully interrogated by Poirot to assess truthfulness related to her testimony."&lt;SEP&gt;"Countess Andrenyi is identified as Mrs. Armstrong's young sister and plays a role in Poirot's inquiry about past recognition by Miss Debenham."&lt;SEP&gt;"Countess Andrenyi is suspected of having ties to an event involving the Armstrong family and is implicated in a plot surrounding the burning of a letter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Countess Andrenyi's involvement is questioned based on alibi evidence like taking a sleeping draught, which suggests she could not have been involved in the crime."&lt;SEP&gt;"Countess Andrenyi's involvement is questioned based on alibi evidence like taking a sleeping draught."&lt;SEP&gt;"Countess Andrenyi's luggage contained a scarlet kimono, which was misused as a red herring in the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Countess Andrenyi, with her Christian name appearing as Elena but possibly meant to be Helena, is suspected of altering her identity. Her luggage label evidence further implicates her in the case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Countess Elena Maria Andrenyi is the wife of Count Andrenyi; she provides information about her whereabouts and habits on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Countess Andrenyi is a character in 'Murder on the Orient Express', identified as Mrs. Armstrong’s sister, with whom Poirot interacts to gather information."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Countess is implicated alongside her husband, with discussions about her innocence and loyalty forming part of the investigation's narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"The wife of Count Andrenyi, revealed as Helena Goldenberg, who has a personal motive connected to a past crime involving a relative."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fd65fe3716ce22231f6ea5162982b25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05861ce1d97b51ee7ba7e14ad6a716ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0979a36edbbd14083fb610d290cd2bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b886ab01915fbe926ed31faaa244ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525a2be9aa2fefc69a55692560d1211f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6002972d88a92a390f28d441cd83a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ee36d6bef7ec1eb1413cc372b39bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d</data>
    </node>
