    <node id="&quot;CASSETTI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cassetti is a person whose sentence of death was escaped and needed to be executed by a group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cassetti is an individual described negatively by Princess Dragomiroff, who suggests she would prefer him dead over any personal interaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cassetti is identified as the real name of the victim in the narrative. Poirot uncovers his true identity, which relates back to an incident involving Daisy Armstrong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cassetti is the target of retribution by the group for escaping a sentence of death, suggesting he was involved in a serious crime against the Armstrongs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cassetti was a kidnapper involved in the Armstrong case, ultimately revealed to be Ratchett."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cassetti, whose real name was exposed as being responsible for the kidnapping of Sonia Armstrong's child in America, is murdered during the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real identity of Ratchett, known to MacQueen through a familial case connection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The real identity of Ratchett, revealed later in the narrative as a man sought for kidnapping and murder related to Daisy Armstrong."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e4b0cbed28fb17eaddac7f89bea44ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d4c5ec355b91832ff6974cba34014c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98cdca9d8857515cf19c2ae06e9d069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e5b19416dc42d6ed9bbd0880c6ecea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdcbbccf1561d4915ce0f64536c1893b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857357aeeee56eaf90ec14021d2a1053</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DAISY ARMSTRONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A child whose kidnapping and murder are central events driving the narrative; she is referred to affectionately by Greta Ohlsson."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daisy Armstrong refers to a character involved in a past case that connects with Cassetti's history and motives for leaving America."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daisy Armstrong was a child kidnapped and murdered, her father Colonel Armstrong and mother Mrs. Armstrong were devastated by this crime."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daisy Armstrong was involved in a kidnapping incident, which indirectly ties Miss Debenham to suspicion due to her prior association with the Armstrong household."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0979a36edbbd14083fb610d290cd2bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca0b6967cd3627682b57dc6562a6d401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e5b19416dc42d6ed9bbd0880c6ecea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE ARMSTRONG KIDNAPPING CASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This refers to a historical case involving Daisy Armstrong, which holds significance in understanding Cassetti’s background and actions leading up to his death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38e5b19416dc42d6ed9bbd0880c6ecea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIRIT STOVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A spirit stove is used by Poirot in an attempt to uncover clues from charred paper; it represents forensic technology applied during the investigation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38e5b19416dc42d6ed9bbd0880c6ecea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CASSETTI (RATCHETT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cassetti, also known as Ratchett, is identified as the murderer of Daisy Armstrong and changed his name after being acquitted due to technicalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONEL ARMSTRONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A former military figure involved in a tragic past event related to Daisy Armstrong's kidnapping and murder, whose legacy is central to the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonel Armstrong is Daisy Armstrong's father, an English V.C., who committed suicide after his daughter's murder and wife's subsequent death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonel Armstrong was a friend of Madame's known from her connections with the actress Linda Arden and his wife, Sonia Armstrong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonel Armstrong was a significant figure connected to the Armstrong case, which is central to the plot on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonel Armstrong was an acquaintance of Princess Dragomiroff, relevant to her background story shared with Poirot."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Colonel Armstrong involved in a shocking affair where his child was kidnapped and killed, discussed by Colonel Arbuthnot."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ca0b6967cd3627682b57dc6562a6d401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70add9ec68a4e0f891845ba07b41bdc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab40254b7af0225a39e56ce1256063e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRS. ARMSTRONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A woman mentioned by MacQueen as gentle and heartbroken; related to a case handled by Mr. MacQueen's father."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mother of Daisy Armstrong and connected to the kidnapping incident. Her past interactions are relevant to Miss Debenham's history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mrs. Armstrong was Daisy Armstrong’s mother, who died following the kidnapping of her daughter and the birth of a stillborn child."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mrs. Armstrong's young sister, known as the Countess Andrenyi, plays a significant role in the mystery surrounding 'Murder on the Orient Express'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mrs. Armstrong’s identity and connections are discussed in relation to Helena Andrenyi, contributing to understanding character relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sister of Helena Goldenberg, whose death is linked to the motive for revenge against Ratchett."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sister of Helena Goldenberg; her murder by Ratchett is a motivating factor in Helena's actions and the case at hand."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b886ab01915fbe926ed31faaa244ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0979a36edbbd14083fb610d290cd2bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdcbbccf1561d4915ce0f64536c1893b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ee36d6bef7ec1eb1413cc372b39bec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE ARMSTRONG BABY CASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Armstrong Baby Case refers to the tragic kidnapping and murder of Daisy Armstrong, sparking public outrage and further tragedy within the family."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W. K. VAN DER HALT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"W. K. Van der Halt was Colonel Armstrong’s maternal grandfather, a Wall Street millionaire."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH OR SWISS NURSEMAID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nursemaid, suspected of having knowledge about the crime but later proven innocent, tragically died by suicide following police pressure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARMSTRONG FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A family mentioned by Count Andrenyi, potentially relevant to his past experiences or connections."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Armstrong family includes Colonel and Mrs. Armstrong and their daughter Daisy; they suffered multiple tragedies related to Daisy's kidnapping and murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Armstrong family includes Colonel and Sonia Armstrong, connected to the kidnapping incident involving Cassetti."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Armstrong family is central to the plot, having suffered a tragedy that leads to a group decision for retribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Armstrong family is referenced regarding a tragic kidnapping and murder case that ties into Poirot's investigation on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Victims of Ratchett, mentioned to establish their background and the motive behind his murder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d4c5ec355b91832ff6974cba34014c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525a2be9aa2fefc69a55692560d1211f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaa6c3abf0bc14e3f3b6ff5944d1913d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSTANTINE, DR.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Constantine is a doctor who joins Poirot and M. Bouc for the inquiry regarding M. Ratchett's death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0499d730557e0cb23aaa505d69d8310f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIERRE MICHEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conductor Pierre Michel is initially suspected in M. Ratchett's murder due to a uniform intended to throw suspicion on him."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mentioned by M. Bouc in connection with a button, suggesting potential involvement in the case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pierre Michel is a train worker whose involvement with the Orient Express was crucial to the timing of the plot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pierre Michel is implicated as part of twelve conspirators due to his connection to a French girl, potentially his daughter, who was murdered in connection with the Armstrong case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pierre Michel is one of the conductors on the Orient Express, described as a big blond conductor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pierre Michel is one of the passengers on the train who saw the woman in a red kimono, contributing to the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pierre Michel is the Wagon Lit conductor, employed for over fifteen years and noted to be honest but not particularly intelligent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pierre Michel is the conductor whose movements are analyzed to understand the presence and actions of the suspicious person on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pierre Michel is the man who made up Monsieur's bed during dinner, observed passenger movement, and confirmed security measures on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Wagon Lit conductor implicated by a button found at the crime scene, claiming innocence and lack of motive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wagon Lit conductor wrongly implicated by a button found at the crime scene, claiming his innocence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43365b2b9f4f112313d61e10bcd53293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc5d82dcccb754c0a3c6b724c659871e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2f47e7e728fa86cdbd201b3054b4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaa6c3abf0bc14e3f3b6ff5944d1913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857357aeeee56eaf90ec14021d2a1053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94520989a3204d455132c5bb78aeef3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0499d730557e0cb23aaa505d69d8310f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN SECRETARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The American Secretary is a young man who visited M. Ratchett’s compartment after his valet, potentially providing insight into events before the murder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0499d730557e0cb23aaa505d69d8310f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VALET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ratchett’s valet is mentioned as a potentially disguised suspect due to his height being compatible with Poirot's hypothesis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Valet attended to M. Ratchett in his compartment shortly before dinner, indicating he was one of the last people present with him."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0499d730557e0cb23aaa505d69d8310f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN LADY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
