      <data key="d2">chunk-0499d730557e0cb23aaa505d69d8310f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONEL MACQUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colonel MacQueen was in his compartment with Mr. Ratchett’s secretary when Pierre Michel made up his bed, potentially a witness to late-night activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0499d730557e0cb23aaa505d69d8310f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MR. RATCHETT/CASSETTI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Identified as a character in 'Murder on the Orient Express', real name is revealed to be Cassetti, involved in an Armstrong kidnapping case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Ratchett is revealed as Cassetti, a notorious criminal involved in kidnapping, particularly related to Daisy Armstrong's case."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc7f212f7cc245171a145500065be35</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONSIEUR POIROT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monsieur Poirot is a detective investigating the murder case aboard the train. He interacts with other characters to gather information and solve the mystery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monsieur Poirot is the detective conducting an investigation on the train, questioning witnesses and examining details of the crime scene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monsieur Poirot is the detective leading the investigation, working on understanding the connections between various characters and evidence in the murder case."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LITTLE DAISY ARMSTRONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Daisy Armstrong was involved in a famous kidnapping case handled by Hector MacQueen’s father; she is mentioned as part of Cassetti's criminal activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VINCOVCI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The last station before the incident discussed in 'Murder on the Orient Express', where the conductor went to check a bell ringing and returned to his seat."&lt;SEP&gt;"The place Mr. MacQueen and Colonel Arbuthnot considered getting off the train, but returned due to cold weather."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vincovci is a location where Colonel Arbuthnot briefly stopped due to a blizzard while traveling on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vincovci is a location where the train stops, providing an opportunity for the crime to be committed as discussed by the characters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vincovci is mentioned as a location in relation to the time of departure from where MacQueen and others parted company for the night."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vincovci is the last stop before the train incident, where conductors noted the platform and locked doors between carriages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6d78fe18a6cdc823562ae23bea032d2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d4cc4a3142e66b8dd0de74d27c22d1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc7f212f7cc245171a145500065be35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94520989a3204d455132c5bb78aeef3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdcbbccf1561d4915ce0f64536c1893b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MR. MACQUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A young American with strong feelings about a case handled by his father, the district attorney; he expresses indignation toward Ratchett/Cassetti."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cdcbbccf1561d4915ce0f64536c1893b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE DISTRICT ATTORNEY&quot;">
