    <node id="&quot;SONIA ARMSTRONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sonia Armstrong is mentioned as the god-daughter of Princess Dragomiroff and a member of the Armstrong family involved in a past tragedy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sonia Armstrong is the wife of Colonel Armstrong and god-daughter to Madame; she has lost her child in a kidnapping orchestrated by Cassetti."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sonia Armstrong was known personally by Princess Dragomiroff. Her relationship with the Princess is mentioned as a point of contrast to the murder victim, Cassetti."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sonia, the daughter of Countess Andrenyi, is adored by Hector MacQueen, indicating personal stakes in the unfolding events related to her family."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98cdca9d8857515cf19c2ae06e9d069</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MADAME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Madame is a passenger on the train, interacting with Hercule Poirot during his investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Madame is an old lady who was acquainted with Colonel and Sonia Armstrong, as well as Linda Arden."&lt;SEP&gt;"Madame refers to a character whose testimony and recognition are being questioned regarding any suspects seen during their travel."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c80e358e965dae0d3f3898628b68de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LINDA ARDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Linda Arden is an acclaimed tragic actress, friend of Madame, and mother of Sonia Armstrong. She lives in retirement due to delicate health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mother of Helena Goldenberg, mentioned as part of her family background."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2b886ab01915fbe926ed31faaa244ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COUNT ANDRENYI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A passenger on the Orient Express involved in executing Cassetti’s death sentence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Count Andrenyi and his wife are discussed regarding their physical characteristics which rule them out for certain disguises."&lt;SEP&gt;"Count Andrenyi holds a diplomatic passport which exempts him from customs examination. He has a truculent disposition and consents to having his luggage searched despite his diplomatic status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Count Andrenyi is a Hungarian diplomat with an alibi for midnight to 2 A.M, except from 1 to 1.15."&lt;SEP&gt;"Count Andrenyi is a well-dressed passenger who is questioned by Hercule Poirot about his knowledge concerning Cassetti and the events of the murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Count Andrenyi is one of the large passengers, possibly relevant to Poirot's theory about disguises."&lt;SEP&gt;"Count Andrenyi is one of the passengers on the Orient Express, involved in the investigation regarding his habits and evidence such as where he keeps his handkerchief."&lt;SEP&gt;"Count Andrenyi takes steps to alter his wife's passport, suggesting involvement in concealing or changing their identities for clandestine reasons."&lt;SEP&gt;"Count Andrenyi, an aristocratic character, discusses his movements during the night of an incident while traveling with his wife, Countess Elena Maria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Count is one of the suspects being investigated by Poirot for his potential involvement in the murder case aboard the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"The husband of Countess Andrenyi, involved in a case surrounding their identity and actions related to a murder on the Orient Express."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2377471b4daac2b86e49ff3b3cd311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b886ab01915fbe926ed31faaa244ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525a2be9aa2fefc69a55692560d1211f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f5533179a24abef3edb831a2667e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6002972d88a92a390f28d441cd83a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857357aeeee56eaf90ec14021d2a1053</data>
    </node>
