    <node id="&quot;ARMSTRONG CASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A past event involving Daisy Armstrong, central to the unfolding narrative of suspicions and confessions on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"A previous criminal case involving Mr. Armstrong that connects to Ratchett's past and possibly to his motives for murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to a kidnapping case involving Gypsy Armstrong, which is connected to the past of Mr. Ratchett (Cassetti)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Armstrong case is central to the narrative, involving an escape from justice by Ratchett and subsequent events leading to his murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Armstrong case refers to a past event involving Colonel Armstrong, central to the plot and connects multiple characters to M. Ratchett’s murder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ca0b6967cd3627682b57dc6562a6d401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70add9ec68a4e0f891845ba07b41bdc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc7f212f7cc245171a145500065be35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739553f4722a651ef8fe4bd2726b6a2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HARDMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A character whose narrative provides context about Ratchett's instructions and potential private enemy, key to understanding motives in the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A passenger who claims to be an operative of a New York detective agency, providing testimony about Ratchett/Cassetti."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hardman fabricated a story about being called by Ratchett, contributing to the deception surrounding the murder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hardman is a character who provided a description of a Wagon Lit attendant, adding to the mystery aboard the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hardman is considered in the investigation but ruled out as a suspect due to his physical height and role on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hardman is not part of the Armstrong household but seems emotionally connected to the French girl who was murdered, suggesting a motive for his involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hardman is ruled out as a suspect due to his physical height and role in the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hardman is traveling with a false passport, making him an object of suspicion. His account of himself is considered reliable by the narrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hardman tracked down Ratchett as part of the plan to execute Cassetti's sentence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mr. Hardman is a character on the train who has an uncertain identity story, which he claims can be confirmed by young MacQueen from New York."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd65fe3716ce22231f6ea5162982b25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d4c5ec355b91832ff6974cba34014c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2f47e7e728fa86cdbd201b3054b4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c1ab2f592fa6c6eb611103748c8a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857357aeeee56eaf90ec14021d2a1053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d</data>
    </node>
