    <node id="&quot;HILDEGARDE SCHMIDT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hildegarde Schmidt is a German subject with no known motive, whose alibi was supported by the conductor and her mistress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hildegarde Schmidt is a maid associated with the letter H and mentioned in relation to an investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hildegarde Schmidt is a maid connected by initial 'H', but eliminated from suspicion based on social class assumptions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hildegarde Schmidt is a passenger on the Orient Express, suspected to be involved due to the discovery of a uniform in her luggage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hildegarde Schmidt is suspected by Poirot of being connected with finding the Wagon Lit conductor's uniform in her luggage if she is guilty."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hildegarde Schmidt is the train attendant and narrator, recounting her experiences and interactions with other passengers aboard the Orient Express while investigating a murder case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hildegarde Schmidt provides testimony that supports the existence of a suspicious man dressed in Wagon Lit uniform, adding credibility to Hardman's account."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hildegarde Schmidt, a maid, is suspected of being more than just a lady’s-maid due to her culinary skills, indicating she might have been involved in the household beyond typical duties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hildegarde Schmidt, the maid connected by initial 'H', is eliminated from suspicion based on assumptions about social class and involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The German maid whose testimony supports the timeline of the murder."</data>
