    <node id="&quot;HERCULE POIROT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Hercule Poirot is a fictional Belgian detective created by Agatha Christie, renowned for his sharp intellect, distinctive methods, and meticulous approach to solving crimes. A former star of the Belgian police force, Poirot is depicted as observant, perceptive, and with keen observation skills, making him a central figure in criminal investigations. Known for his methodical inquiry and attention to detail, he focuses on character assessment and guides others toward confession while pursuing the truth.

In Agatha Christie's "Murder on the Orient Express," Poirot is hired by the Compagnie Internationale des Wagons Lits to investigate the murder of M. Ratchett (formerly Cassetti) aboard the train. His reputation as an international detective with distinctive investigative skills leads him through interactions with various passengers, including Count and Countess Andrenyi, and Miss Debenham, gathering information relevant to solving the mystery.

Throughout his journey on the Orient Express, Poirot observes events, manages unexpected developments in his schedule, and deduces the complex events surrounding the murder. His inquiries reveal not only the identity of the victim but also challenge simple theories proposed by others, such as M. Bouc's theory about the crime. Known for solving mysteries using keen intuition and deep thought, Poirot's investigation on the train exemplifies his intellectual prowess and methodical nature in detective work.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ed48a0164410cf91af70de10aa682c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca0b6967cd3627682b57dc6562a6d401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70add9ec68a4e0f891845ba07b41bdc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6425d97244d2e1b3ba2690d999ff90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1716f8bcc2163e8b92452e6f73b77a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e6b35b92b29b3dc0f3f2552de9e690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0979a36edbbd14083fb610d290cd2bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e4b0cbed28fb17eaddac7f89bea44ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98cdca9d8857515cf19c2ae06e9d069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525a2be9aa2fefc69a55692560d1211f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04cc4e61491a2625d57ae93577180429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c2fe5c17ad711c386f6cdce1c5b966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ee36d6bef7ec1eb1413cc372b39bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02cf2a88ee1b375e65a1e1e19c6b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90462864ccc3552f8203a4d315744169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e2be2103dbf9128ae4cbba4b8804c3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c80f04908bd81829962c824002084f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43365b2b9f4f112313d61e10bcd53293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee68b60e91d3765c877c8570ac90496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1217d5c8472eb8a31ffda2c871e44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab40254b7af0225a39e56ce1256063e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c80e358e965dae0d3f3898628b68de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c079a095f377928fe8ac396a4a1a138a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828593a23e34b4ef40681f2f1551531c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c1ab2f592fa6c6eb611103748c8a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6002972d88a92a390f28d441cd83a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94520989a3204d455132c5bb78aeef3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a3febbe10401ac2c84958f17348e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGATHA CHRISTIE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Agatha Christie is a renowned mystery writer whose books have sold over two billion copies globally. She authored 79 novels, numerous short stories, and plays. Christie is particularly famous for creating the beloved detective character Hercule Poirot, who features prominently in her works, including the acclaimed novel "Murder on the Orient Express." This detective novel involves a gripping murder mystery that unfolds during a train journey. The story includes key characters such as Hercule Poirot and Mary Debenham, alongside others like M. Bouc, each playing significant roles in unraveling the intricate plot. Christie's expertise in crafting complex narratives involving mystery and detective elements is evident throughout her body of work, with "Murder on the Orient Express" being a prime example that showcases her talent for engaging readers in suspenseful and cleverly constructed tales. Her influence and contributions to the genre are central to this text's context, underscoring her status as one of the most prominent authors in detective fiction.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e00f6f5a5a46007fccdffb363d3da9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ed48a0164410cf91af70de10aa682c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6425d97244d2e1b3ba2690d999ff90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e6b35b92b29b3dc0f3f2552de9e690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc5d82dcccb754c0a3c6b724c659871e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0979a36edbbd14083fb610d290cd2bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a9342d0705844f8f1ea629e4f03a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca27d922d6c043dfba49b489cbb113a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37c5026a1b7465a5dd9fa6a338677957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45ee86f6e6f6be3d0eecd889335cf58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-854a7ec825bca51df1d6a969ff1fe76e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99aab564ce73aa4ab62ffefe074192dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e4b0cbed28fb17eaddac7f89bea44ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98cdca9d8857515cf19c2ae06e9d069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3903f6b9b84f9e5314a864e236cf0871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525a2be9aa2fefc69a55692560d1211f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c2fe5c17ad711c386f6cdce1c5b966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ee36d6bef7ec1eb1413cc372b39bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc7f212f7cc245171a145500065be35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2377471b4daac2b86e49ff3b3cd311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaa6c3abf0bc14e3f3b6ff5944d1913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab40254b7af0225a39e56ce1256063e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b935beff32f900e8b2f9a059a1a90d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c80e358e965dae0d3f3898628b68de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e5b19416dc42d6ed9bbd0880c6ecea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c1ab2f592fa6c6eb611103748c8a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94520989a3204d455132c5bb78aeef3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a3febbe10401ac2c84958f17348e98</data>
