    <node id="&quot;MURDER ON THE ORIENT EXPRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Murder on the Orient Express" is a renowned detective fiction novel by Agatha Christie. It revolves around an intricate murder mystery set aboard the famed Orient Express train during its journey from Istanbul to Calais. The story features Hercule Poirot, a distinguished Belgian detective, who leads the investigation into the murder of a man known as Ratchett. As the plot unfolds, Poirot finds himself navigating through complex motives and interactions among multiple passengers on the train, each serving as potential suspects or witnesses. This novel is celebrated for its gripping narrative, memorable characters, and engaging mystery that captivates readers from start to finish. Christie's storytelling prowess shines in this work, making "Murder on the Orient Express" a hallmark of detective fiction.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ed48a0164410cf91af70de10aa682c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd65fe3716ce22231f6ea5162982b25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc69e98e6913ae79fe45aa1a57ea357e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e6b35b92b29b3dc0f3f2552de9e690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc5d82dcccb754c0a3c6b724c659871e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0979a36edbbd14083fb610d290cd2bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a9342d0705844f8f1ea629e4f03a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa8804f1ac20b273870388b80bf8f66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdcbbccf1561d4915ce0f64536c1893b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0499d730557e0cb23aaa505d69d8310f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-854a7ec825bca51df1d6a969ff1fe76e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99aab564ce73aa4ab62ffefe074192dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e4b0cbed28fb17eaddac7f89bea44ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ee36d6bef7ec1eb1413cc372b39bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43365b2b9f4f112313d61e10bcd53293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b5b38b2dd23c77b4817324b15fd3d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0262591c0f7139618aa8ff97ba9028ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1217d5c8472eb8a31ffda2c871e44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2f47e7e728fa86cdbd201b3054b4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e5b19416dc42d6ed9bbd0880c6ecea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c1ab2f592fa6c6eb611103748c8a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a3febbe10401ac2c84958f17348e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONEL ARBUTHNOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Colonel Arbuthnot is a British Colonel returning from India, serving as a passenger aboard the Orient Express. Described as a tall man between forty and fifty years old with a reserved demeanor, he has military ties suggesting loyalty within his social circle, including an association with the Armstrongs. Despite being suspected due to various circumstances such as possessing a pipe-cleaner linked to the crime scene, and exhibiting protective behavior towards Miss Mary Debenham, he is considered unlikely to be involved in the murder of M. Ratchett due to cultural stereotypes and other exonerating evidence.

Colonel Arbuthnot converses with various passengers, including MacQueen and Miss Debenham, discussing topics ranging from world politics to policies in India, reflecting his preference for law over private vengeance. His testimony is crucial as he provides an alibi for Hector MacQueen during the murder and recalls observations of a suspicious man on the train, aligning with other witness accounts.

Despite showing reluctance to cooperate fully with Poirot's investigation and appearing defensive about his relationship with Miss Debenham—whom he claims just met despite seeming familiarity—Arbuthnot’s integrity is repeatedly highlighted. His participation in events such as following Miss Debenham out of the restaurant car underscores his involvement in the unfolding mystery, yet his interactions raise suspicions without confirming any wrongdoing.

Overall, Colonel Arbuthnot emerges as a complex character involved in the central mystery on the Orient Express, balancing between being a protective acquaintance and a potential suspect whose alibi and integrity ultimately suggest his innocence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e00f6f5a5a46007fccdffb363d3da9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d4cc4a3142e66b8dd0de74d27c22d1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1716f8bcc2163e8b92452e6f73b77a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f56d007fba699897f7e8d88951c40f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0979a36edbbd14083fb610d290cd2bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af707c4982d5d13c07eb2929dad417be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdcbbccf1561d4915ce0f64536c1893b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e4b0cbed28fb17eaddac7f89bea44ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98cdca9d8857515cf19c2ae06e9d069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a290cdc5cb69e2a286069c682ea93990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ee36d6bef7ec1eb1413cc372b39bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857357aeeee56eaf90ec14021d2a1053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02cf2a88ee1b375e65a1e1e19c6b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90462864ccc3552f8203a4d315744169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee68b60e91d3765c877c8570ac90496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b5b38b2dd23c77b4817324b15fd3d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0262591c0f7139618aa8ff97ba9028ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab40254b7af0225a39e56ce1256063e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef2a5be101e1bcbe764f5cc6a651113&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c80e358e965dae0d3f3898628b68de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2f47e7e728fa86cdbd201b3054b4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f5533179a24abef3edb831a2667e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94520989a3204d455132c5bb78aeef3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6002972d88a92a390f28d441cd83a51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POIROT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Hercule Poirot is a renowned Belgian detective character created by Agatha Christie, known for his sharp intellect, keen observation, and methodical approach to solving complex mysteries. Central to the novel "Murder on the Orient Express," Poirot investigates the murder of Mr. Ratchett aboard the luxurious train journey from Istanbul to Calais. As a central figure in this gripping tale, Poirot listens to various passengers' accounts, including Mrs. Hubbard's, and meticulously analyzes inconsistencies among their testimonies.

Throughout his investigation, Poirot interacts with other characters such as M. Bouc, Dr. Constantine, Colonel Arbuthnot, Greta Ohlsson, Masterman, the Count and Countess Andrenyi, Antonio Foscarelli, and Mr. Hardman. He conducts interviews to gather evidence, questioning each passenger's whereabouts and observations during key moments of the crime. Poirot examines physical clues like a handkerchief, pipe-cleaner, scarlet kimono, and a broken watch, showcasing his investigative prowess.

Known for presenting multiple plausible solutions to the murder case, Poirot challenges initial theories—such as M. Bouc's suspicion of an Italian suspect—and eventually unravels the intricately planned crime. He perceives the investigation as a jigsaw puzzle, where every piece must be scrutinized before forming conclusions. His interactions with passengers often occur in communal spaces like the restaurant car or while examining luggage and the crime scene.

In addition to his detective skills, Poirot is depicted as compassionate and engaged, helping M. Bouc with travel arrangements and even demonstrating knowledge of literature, such as works by Dickens. Overall, Hercule Poirot's character exemplifies logical reasoning and a profound commitment to justice, making him one of Agatha Christie's most iconic detectives.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6d78fe18a6cdc823562ae23bea032d2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d4cc4a3142e66b8dd0de74d27c22d1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc69e98e6913ae79fe45aa1a57ea357e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f56d007fba699897f7e8d88951c40f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af707c4982d5d13c07eb2929dad417be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a9342d0705844f8f1ea629e4f03a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97f221cfcb44e82fc16604e8188110e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a03ffacff7379d0f671e5dac524569f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca27d922d6c043dfba49b489cbb113a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdcbbccf1561d4915ce0f64536c1893b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37c5026a1b7465a5dd9fa6a338677957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0499d730557e0cb23aaa505d69d8310f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-854a7ec825bca51df1d6a969ff1fe76e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05861ce1d97b51ee7ba7e14ad6a716ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73450c21b26b1c97cae9c9cc4f33121&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43365b2b9f4f112313d61e10bcd53293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc7f212f7cc245171a145500065be35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b886ab01915fbe926ed31faaa244ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b5b38b2dd23c77b4817324b15fd3d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739553f4722a651ef8fe4bd2726b6a2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2377471b4daac2b86e49ff3b3cd311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaa6c3abf0bc14e3f3b6ff5944d1913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a74ad1f7a65a442e84243a05d21bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab40254b7af0225a39e56ce1256063e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-943f6d42e5d505073e2dc802d2e65542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d4c5ec355b91832ff6974cba34014c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7a4bf22d1e71c2aa1f0dd57e612483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef2a5be101e1bcbe764f5cc6a651113&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2f47e7e728fa86cdbd201b3054b4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f52cbd857b4ec571997368d76d3ad4f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e5b19416dc42d6ed9bbd0880c6ecea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f5533179a24abef3edb831a2667e0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRINCESS DRAGOMIROFF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Princess Natalia Dragomiroff, often referred to as "her Excellency" or "Madame la Princesse," is an elderly Russian aristocrat and a dignified passenger on the Orient Express. Despite her unattractive appearance, she exudes strength of character and has amassed considerable wealth by investing her late husband's fortune abroad. As a naturalized French subject, she shares a close bond with the Armstrong family, being intimately acquainted and godmother to Sonia Armstrong.

Princess Dragomiroff is significantly involved in the investigation into a murder aboard the train, owing to possessing a handkerchief that plays a crucial role in unraveling the mystery and highlighting loyalty dynamics. This involvement also connects her to Countess Helena, who recognizes her significance due to past events related to the narrative. Despite being considered for suspicion due to her strong influence on those around her, evidence of her whereabouts, physical attributes, and a solid alibi from midnight to 2 A.M. work in her favor to clear her name.

Throughout the investigation, she interacts assertively with the staff and is recognized by notable figures such as Poirot and M. Bouc. Her presence in the conspiracy against Ratchett adds complexity to her character, yet her calm demeanor, devotion to her maid, and pride in justice suggest a more profound moral standing. Although initially viewed as potentially biased regarding the murder discussed during the inquiry, she eventually considers Poirot's explanations about her maid’s evidence and alibi.

Despite her frail physique and refusal to write with her hand—leading to discussions about her capability to inflict certain wounds—Princess Dragomiroff maintains a dignified composure. Her involvement in the execution plot alongside other passengers further cements her role as an important figure within this intricate mystery, while her social standing and alibi contribute to her eventual consideration beyond suspicion.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-857357aeeee56eaf90ec14021d2a1053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e00f6f5a5a46007fccdffb363d3da9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd65fe3716ce22231f6ea5162982b25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99aab564ce73aa4ab62ffefe074192dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e904a20881c2e14b8e26d8f332bf9bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98cdca9d8857515cf19c2ae06e9d069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2377471b4daac2b86e49ff3b3cd311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b5b38b2dd23c77b4817324b15fd3d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aabf3f278593d24c8e7cd53fbcd961f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97f221cfcb44e82fc16604e8188110e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739553f4722a651ef8fe4bd2726b6a2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37c5026a1b7465a5dd9fa6a338677957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f5533179a24abef3edb831a2667e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRS. HUBBARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Mrs. Hubbard is a character aboard the Orient Express, portrayed as an American lady known for both her loquacious nature and unusual quietness during a pivotal investigation, suggesting her involvement in unfolding events related to Mr. Ratchett's murder case. A passenger connected by the initial "H," she interacts closely with other passengers, including offering comfort to Greta Ohlsson and providing evidence about the crime's timeline to Poirot.

Throughout the narrative, Mrs. Hubbard is depicted as someone who experiences emotional vulnerability, requiring comfort such as tea or coffee in scenes with Poirot. She becomes notably distressed upon discovering a bloodied knife, leading to her fainting—an event that contributes significantly to the investigation. Despite this shock, she actively participates by offering aspirin to Greta Ohlsson and shares details about her journey to the East, expressing fear towards Ratchett.

Mrs. Hubbard claims to have seen a man in her compartment, an assertion that initiates an altercation with the conductor and sets off the chain of events leading to the murder investigation. Her locked compartment door plays a crucial role, as it serves as a passageway for others entering Ratchett's darkened room where he was murdered. Despite having no known motive, Mrs. Hubbard is surrounded by suspicious circumstances due to her claims about a man in her compartment and her potentially false account of the status of a door bolt, which contradicts physical evidence.

Further contributing to Poirot’s investigation, she mentions finding a button in her compartment that supports other testimonies regarding the crime. As someone with acting skills, possibly related to Mrs. Armstrong as her mother, she plays an instrumental role in executing a plan against Cassetti (Ratchett). Her character embodies complexity and intrigue, being both a source of valuable insights and questionable actions within the murder mystery aboard the Orient Express.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ed48a0164410cf91af70de10aa682c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd65fe3716ce22231f6ea5162982b25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc69e98e6913ae79fe45aa1a57ea357e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f56d007fba699897f7e8d88951c40f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af707c4982d5d13c07eb2929dad417be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca27d922d6c043dfba49b489cbb113a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97f221cfcb44e82fc16604e8188110e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a03ffacff7379d0f671e5dac524569f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45ee86f6e6f6be3d0eecd889335cf58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-854a7ec825bca51df1d6a969ff1fe76e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9852ab845971db75c2a83895116dfabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e73450c21b26b1c97cae9c9cc4f33121&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04cc4e61491a2625d57ae93577180429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90462864ccc3552f8203a4d315744169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739553f4722a651ef8fe4bd2726b6a2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee1f9ebf14192e2e1ce8e0eee9949ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2377471b4daac2b86e49ff3b3cd311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaa6c3abf0bc14e3f3b6ff5944d1913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a74ad1f7a65a442e84243a05d21bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef2a5be101e1bcbe764f5cc6a651113&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2f47e7e728fa86cdbd201b3054b4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e5b19416dc42d6ed9bbd0880c6ecea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f5533179a24abef3edb831a2667e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c1ab2f592fa6c6eb611103748c8a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6002972d88a92a390f28d441cd83a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a3febbe10401ac2c84958f17348e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RATCHETT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Ratchett, whose real identity is revealed as Cassetti, plays a pivotal role in the narrative surrounding his death aboard the Orient Express. A victim of murder, Ratchett's demise forms the core investigation led by Detective Hercule Poirot. Known for his wealth and status, which allowed him to escape justice for past crimes in America—including being found guilty in connection with the kidnapping of Sonia Armstrong’s child—Ratchett lived under an alias due to these criminal associations.

Before embarking on the fateful journey on the Orient Express, Ratchett engaged Hercule Poirot's services for protection against perceived enemies, revealing his concerns about safety. This involvement highlights both his wealthy status and potential threats he faced. Additionally, a valet attended to him as an absent passenger, suggesting his importance or adding to the mystery surrounding him.

Ratchett’s past actions had significant repercussions; notably, they motivated Helena Goldenberg's determination to seek justice against him for his role in the Armstrong case. Prior to the train murder, Ratchett received threatening letters and one specific letter about the Armstrong baby—linking directly back to his criminal history.

On the night of his death, Ratchett resided in a compartment adjacent to Poirot’s on the Stamboul-Calais carriage. The investigation into his murder revealed he was killed by one or more individuals, with discussions about his identity and the motives for his murder being central to solving the crime. His death, discussed with approval by MacQueen, indicates that while controversial, it was considered a form of justice by some.

Ratchett's last moments were spent in bed, having been read to by Greta Ohlsson shortly before 10:40, found dead later with a sleeping draught beside him. This detail adds to the mystery and complexity of his murder investigation on the Orient Express, which becomes central to Poirot’s unraveling narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ed48a0164410cf91af70de10aa682c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd65fe3716ce22231f6ea5162982b25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca0b6967cd3627682b57dc6562a6d401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a9342d0705844f8f1ea629e4f03a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97f221cfcb44e82fc16604e8188110e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdcbbccf1561d4915ce0f64536c1893b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e4b0cbed28fb17eaddac7f89bea44ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04cc4e61491a2625d57ae93577180429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c992fd77a9a07d04ba95f4a1c5b07f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857357aeeee56eaf90ec14021d2a1053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02cf2a88ee1b375e65a1e1e19c6b6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43365b2b9f4f112313d61e10bcd53293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38228728b48209be2f7a1ae5bf4db339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b886ab01915fbe926ed31faaa244ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b5b38b2dd23c77b4817324b15fd3d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739553f4722a651ef8fe4bd2726b6a2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aabf3f278593d24c8e7cd53fbcd961f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaa6c3abf0bc14e3f3b6ff5944d1913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffec81d1a6e4064edf1aa47ab020e43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703d5601a02c4e426e36dea49d88820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d4c5ec355b91832ff6974cba34014c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef2a5be101e1bcbe764f5cc6a651113&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f2f47e7e728fa86cdbd201b3054b4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6002972d88a92a390f28d441cd83a51</data>
