      <data key="d3">149.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Hercule Poirot collaborates with M. Bouc to uncover the truth behind Ratchett's murder on the Orient Express."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc and Hercule Poirot share an old acquaintance from their time at the Belgian police force and reunite during travel arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc assists Hercule Poirot throughout the investigation on the Orient Express by providing support and admiration for Poirot's methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc assists and supports Poirot’s investigation by managing the situation on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc discusses the investigation with Hercule Poirot, providing insights and expressing concerns about alerting suspects."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc discusses with Poirot about the details of the Armstrong Baby Case and agrees on the necessity of justice for Cassetti."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc engages Hercule Poirot and his services to investigate the crime on the Orient Express."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc engages with Poirot in discussions about the complexities and progress of the murder investigation on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc enlists Poirot to lead the investigation into M. Ratchett's murder due to his renowned investigative skills."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc is collaborating with Hercule Poirot to solve the murder case on the Orient Express."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc provides observational insights but relies on Poirot's expertise for the final analysis of the crime, acknowledging his role in elucidating crimes is secondary to Poirot’s."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc unexpectedly reunites with Poirot at the Tokatlian Hotel, indicating a professional connection between them related to their work for the Compagnie Internationale des Wagons Lits."&lt;SEP&gt;"M. Bouc works alongside Hercule Poirot in investigating and solving the crime on the Orient Express."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poiroc collaborates with M. Bouc to manage the complexities of searching luggage and dealing with diplomatic considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poirot and M. Bouc work together on the train to investigate a crime, with M. Bouc supporting Poirot's inquiries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poirot guides M. Bouc by affirming and subtly encouraging him to present his thoughts as expected, setting the stage for further discussion on solving the crime."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poirot is informed by M. Bouc about a mysterious incident that has occurred on the Orient Express."</data>
