    <edge source="&quot;AGATHA CHRISTIE&quot;" target="&quot;MURDER ON THE ORIENT EXPRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">117.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"'MURDER ON THE ORIENT EXPRESS' is one of Agatha Christie's most celebrated works, featuring Hercule Poirot as the detective."&lt;SEP&gt;"'Murder on the Orient Express' is a novel authored by Agatha Christie depicting a murder investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie authored 'Murder on the Orient Express', a novel that features a murder mystery set aboard the train, linking the author directly to this significant work."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie authored 'Murder on the Orient Express', featuring a complex mystery involving characters like Hercule Poirot and Countess Andrenyi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie authored 'Murder on the Orient Express', setting the narrative context for the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie authored 'Murder on the Orient Express', which revolves around a murder mystery on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie authored 'Murder on the Orient Express,' where Poirot solves a complex murder mystery aboard the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie authored the novel 'MURDER ON THE ORIENT EXPRESS,' which is central to this text analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agatha Christie is the author who created the novel 'Murder on the Orient Express,' featuring a murder mystery on the train."&lt;SEP&gt;"As the author of the work, Agatha Christie crafts the narrative and constructs the mystery that unfolds within it, defining its characters and plot developments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The novel 'Murder on the Orient Express' is authored by Agatha Christie and sets up the narrative for this mystery involving multiple characters."</data>
